The concrete race is now clear: the test bounded readiness by scheduler turns (`10,000 × Task.yield()`), so under executor load it could exhaust its counter before the command task acquired the actor and published resource ownership. The production path already waits for both task-group children before cleanup; I’m replacing the test’s scheduler-count guess with an explicit actor event and turning the cancellation case into a 50-case parallel stress test while retaining exact cleanup assertions.
